{"_meta": {"backend": "", "recorded": "live", "date": "2026-10-04", "agent_version": "2.27.1", "note": "Captured off the wire on 2026-10-04 for the MCP-app media-delivery RFC's question Q2a (does an MCP tool result's structuredContent reach the model on kiro-cli?): `kiro-cli acp` 2.27.1 driven over stdio, agent-to-client lines in order, through a throwaway workspace agent (includeMcpJson false) whose only tools are one stdio MCP server, with model routing left at auto and the server's tools pre-trusted, so no session/request_permission frame occurs. The server's probe_lookup returns a fresh random sentinel ONLY in structuredContent ({\"record\": {\"value\": <sentinel>}}), with the neutral text \"Lookup finished.\" as its content; probe_control returns a different sentinel inside its content text and is the control. The prompt asked the agent to call probe_lookup once, then probe_control once, then repeat verbatim every identifier, field and value each tool returned, including any structured data. Result for this variant: the structuredContent sentinel appeared in the final assistant text in 0 of 3 valid runs (0 of 3 further valid runs with an outputSchema declared on probe_lookup), while the control sentinel appeared in 3 of 3; the reply here says probe_lookup returned plain text only. Separately, kiro-cli's own report to the client does not carry it either: the tool_call_update rawOutput holds the content items only, with no structuredContent key. In this run the structuredContent sentinel was SENTINEL-81cb33575a024af390ef22d0a3463258, which occurs nowhere in these frames, and the control was SENTINEL-7bb5856efc244ea1943c472432000ed5. Reductions: the _kiro.dev/* notifications other than the tool_call_chunk updates are left out (commands/available x3, mcp/server_initialized x2, metadata x4, subagent/list_update x1), as in session.jsonl: commands/available and metadata describe the recording host, and none is a shape this scenario pins; the session id is replaced with the synthetic kiro-session-1; session/new modes emptied and models cut to the auto routing entry with an empty description, as in session.jsonl; no agent_thought_chunk frames were sent. The probe server and the driver are not in the repository; this note is their specification."}}
